{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The style layer’s predicate.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["occ"],"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"@property"},{"text":" (","kind":"text"},{"text":"nonatomic","kind":"keyword"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"c:objc(cs)NSPredicate","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"NSPredicate"},{"text":" * ","kind":"text"},{"text":"predicate","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":";"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the style layer’s predicate to include only the features in the source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"layer that satisfy a condition that you define. If the style layer initially"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"comes from the style, its predicate corresponds to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"filter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property in the style JSON."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See the “"},{"type":"text","text":"Predicates and Expressions"},{"type":"text","text":"”"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"guide for details about the predicate syntax supported by this class."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Example","text":"Example"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To filter the layer to include only the features whose ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"index"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute is 5"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or 10 and whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ele"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute is at least 1,500, you could create an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSCompoundPredicate"},{"type":"text","text":" along these lines:"}]},{"type":"code